  "worked_solution": "The set of all points $(x,y)$ that are a distance of $8$ units from the origin defines a circle with radius $r=8$ centered at the origin, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/9490799dc8048e1ff6ef30d933afd909cb4932bbe4a4d20cc6b6192384c30554.png)\n\nSo, the required equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={8}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
